n) to fold. Checking allows me to win the current pot (taking the chip lead) if my hand is good, without risking more chips on a dangerous board.\n\nReason: The board is wet with flush and straight possibilities completed on the river. I have strong showdown value with Trip 8s but betting is risky as it could isolate me against better hands or fold out worse ones. Checking ensures I realize my equity and likely win the pot to regain the chip lead.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
